#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:1
msgid "Decide whether to adopt C4 model diagrams in ADRs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:3
msgid "Status: proposed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:4
msgid "Date: 2026-09-19"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:5
msgid "Decision-makers: tkoyama010"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:7
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:9
msgid ""
"ADRs in `docs/decisions/` record *why* a decision was made "
"([ADR-0000](0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md)), but "
"the structure they decide about is described almost entirely in prose. "
"Where a diagram has helped, it was drawn ad hoc: [ADR-0009](0009-decide-"
"how-to-sync-github-repository-settings-with-terraform.md) embeds a "
"Mermaid `sequenceDiagram`, and `slides/slides.md` carries several more. "
"Nothing says what a diagram in an ADR is supposed to show, at which level"
" of abstraction, or with which vocabulary, so two records that both draw "
"\"the architecture\" can disagree about what counts as a box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:11
msgid ""
"The [C4 model](https://c4model.com/) is a candidate vocabulary: it fixes "
"four zoom levels — System Context, Container, Component, Code — and a "
"small element set (person, software system, container, component) that "
"keeps every diagram's boxes comparable. pyvista-wasm has a genuinely "
"layered architecture to describe — a Python-facing PyVista API "
"(`src/pyvista_wasm/`), a TypeScript glue layer (`ts/renderer.ts`), the "
"vtk-wasm module it drives, and the in-browser Python runtime that hosts "
"them — which is exactly the shape C4's Context and Container levels exist"
" to draw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:13
msgid ""
"Should pyvista-wasm adopt C4 as the notation for architecture diagrams in"
" ADRs, and if so, with which toolchain?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:15
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:17
msgid ""
"**Shared vocabulary across records**: Diagrams drawn by different "
"contributors in different ADRs should use the same element types and the "
"same levels, so a reader can compare them without re-learning the "
"notation each time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:18
msgid ""
"**Plain text under version control**: Diagrams must be diffable Markdown "
"that travels through the same PR review flow as the record itself "
"([ADR-0000](0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md)). Binary"
" images or an external editor would break that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:19
msgid ""
"**No new toolchain in CI**: Documentation is built by Sphinx on Read the "
"Docs for every PR. A notation that requires a JVM, Docker, or Graphviz in"
" the docs build is a disproportionate cost for a small project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:20
msgid ""
"**Rendering in the published docs**: ADRs are published alongside the "
"rest of `docs/`. A diagram that renders on GitHub but not on Read the "
"Docs (or the reverse) is only half a diagram."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:21
msgid ""
"**Low authoring overhead**: Records must stay cheap to write. If drawing "
"the diagram costs more than writing the decision, contributors will skip "
"it and the notation will not stick."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:22
msgid ""
"**Right level of abstraction**: The useful levels here are Context (who "
"uses pyvista-wasm and what it depends on) and Container (Python API, "
"TypeScript glue, vtk-wasm, browser runtime). Diagrams of individual "
"classes duplicate the code and rot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:24
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:26
msgid "**Option A: Status quo — ad-hoc Mermaid diagrams, no C4 notation**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:27
msgid "**Option B: Adopt C4 notation using the existing Mermaid toolchain**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:28
msgid ""
"**Option C: Adopt C4 with Structurizr DSL as the model source, with ADRs "
"linked into the model**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:29
msgid "**Option D: Adopt C4 with PlantUML and the C4-PlantUML standard library**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:31
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:33
msgid ""
"Chosen option: \"**Option B: Adopt C4 notation using the existing Mermaid"
" toolchain**\", because it is the only option that gives ADRs a shared "
"architectural vocabulary without adding anything to the documentation "
"build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:35
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The toolchain is already in place and already proven for ADRs: "
"`sphinxcontrib.mermaid` is enabled in `docs/conf.py`, pinned as a docs "
"dependency in `pyproject.toml` (`sphinxcontrib-mermaid>=2.0.0,<3.0.0`, "
"resolved to 2.1.1 in `uv.lock`), and [ADR-0009](0009-decide-how-to-sync-"
"github-repository-settings-with-terraform.md) already renders a "
"`{mermaid}` block through it. The extension defaults `mermaid_version` to"
" 11.12.1 and `docs/conf.py` does not override it, so the Mermaid release "
"loaded in the published docs is one that ships the "
"`C4Context`/`C4Container`/`C4Component` diagram types. Slidev loads its "
"own Mermaid (`mermaid` `^11.16.1` in `slides/package.json`), so the same "
"C4 source can be pasted into the deck without a second notation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:37
msgid ""
"Options C and D both add a runtime the project does not otherwise need — "
"a JVM plus Structurizr Lite, or Java plus Graphviz plus `sphinxcontrib-"
"plantuml` — to buy model-level features (a single model rendered into "
"many views, Structurizr's `!adrs` integration) that a repository with a "
"dozen ADRs does not yet need. Option A is what the project does today and"
" is what prompted the question."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:39
msgid "Adopting C4 means, concretely:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:41
msgid ""
"When an ADR needs an architecture diagram, it is drawn in C4 notation at "
"**System Context** or **Container** level. Component level is used only "
"when the decision is genuinely about internal structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:42
msgid ""
"**Code level is never drawn.** The type stub "
"`src/pyvista_wasm/__init__.pyi` and the API reference built by "
"`autosummary` already describe that level and stay correct automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:43
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Diagrams stay inside the ADR that needs them, in a `{mermaid}` block. "
"There is no central model file to keep in sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:44
msgid ""
"ADRs without an architectural component (tooling, process, documentation "
"decisions) still need no diagram. C4 is a notation to use when drawing, "
"not an obligation to draw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:46
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:48
msgid ""
"Good, because architecture diagrams across ADRs become comparable: the "
"same element types at the same two levels, instead of whatever shape each"
" record invented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:49
msgid ""
"Good, because nothing is added to the docs build — no new dependency, no "
"JVM, no Graphviz — so Read the Docs previews keep working unchanged on "
"every PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:50
msgid ""
"Good, because the diagram source is Markdown inside the record, so it is "
"reviewed in the same diff as the decision it illustrates and cannot drift"
" into a separate artifact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:51
msgid ""
"Good, because the same C4 source can be reused in `slides/slides.md`, "
"which already renders Mermaid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:52
msgid ""
"Bad, because Mermaid's C4 diagram support is flagged experimental "
"upstream: its syntax may change between Mermaid releases, and "
"`mermaid_version` is unpinned in `docs/conf.py`, so a future default bump"
" could alter or break rendering. The mitigation is cheap — pin "
"`mermaid_version` if that ever happens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:53
msgid ""
"Bad, because Mermaid offers little layout control for C4 diagrams "
"compared with Structurizr or PlantUML, so large diagrams look worse. This"
" pushes records toward few, small diagrams, which is the intended outcome"
" anyway."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:54
msgid ""
"Bad, because with no central model, an element that appears in two ADRs "
"can be described inconsistently. Accepted: records are immutable "
"decisions in time, not a live model, and Option C remains available if a "
"live model is ever wanted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:55
msgid ""
"Neutral, because existing non-C4 diagrams (the `sequenceDiagram` in "
"[ADR-0009](0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repository-settings-with-"
"terraform.md), the deck's diagrams) are not retrofitted. C4 governs "
"*architecture* diagrams; sequence and flow diagrams remain the right tool"
" for showing a workflow over time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:57
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:59
msgid ""
"This decision is confirmed by the documentation build, not by inspection:"
" the diagram below is a C4 System Context diagram of pyvista-wasm, and "
"the Read the Docs preview built for the pull request that introduces this"
" record must render it. If it does not render, Mermaid's experimental C4 "
"support is not usable here and this record should be rejected rather than"
" merged with a broken diagram."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:81
msgid ""
"Thereafter, compliance is a review concern: a PR that adds an "
"architecture diagram to an ADR in notation other than C4, or that draws "
"Code-level structure, contradicts this record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:83
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:85
msgid "Option A: Status quo — ad-hoc Mermaid diagrams, no C4 notation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:87
msgid ""
"What the project does today: a `sequenceDiagram` in [ADR-0009](0009"
"-decide-how-to-sync-github-repository-settings-with-terraform.md), flow "
"and sequence diagrams in `slides/slides.md`, no rule about architecture "
"diagrams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:89
msgid ""
"Good, because it has zero cost: nothing to adopt, nothing to learn, "
"nothing to configure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:90
msgid ""
"Good, because Mermaid's non-C4 diagram types are stable and render "
"reliably in both Sphinx and Slidev."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:91
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it is not *wrong* — a small project can carry "
"architecture in prose for a long time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:92
msgid ""
"Bad, because the level of abstraction is decided per diagram, so records "
"cannot be compared and readers must re-orient in each one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:93
msgid ""
"Bad, because nothing distinguishes \"a system\", \"a deployable unit\", "
"and \"a module\" in a project whose whole story is the boundary between "
"Python, TypeScript, and WebAssembly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:95
msgid "Option B: Adopt C4 notation using the existing Mermaid toolchain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:97
msgid ""
"C4 vocabulary expressed in Mermaid `C4Context` / `C4Container` blocks, "
"rendered by the already-enabled `sphinxcontrib.mermaid`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:99
msgid ""
"Good, because the toolchain already exists and is already used by an ADR,"
" so adoption costs one paragraph in this record and nothing in CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:100
msgid ""
"Good, because C4's four levels give an explicit answer to \"how far "
"should I zoom\", which is the question the status quo leaves open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:101
msgid ""
"Good, because the notation is small: contributors need four element "
"types, not a diagramming language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:102
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it provides notation only, not a model — there is no "
"validation that two diagrams describe the same system consistently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:103
msgid ""
"Bad, because Mermaid's C4 support is experimental upstream and its layout"
" engine is weak for anything beyond a modest diagram."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:105
msgid ""
"Option C: Adopt C4 with Structurizr DSL as the model source, with ADRs "
"linked into the model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:107
msgid ""
"[Structurizr](https://structurizr.com/) DSL describes the system once as "
"a model; views are generated from it. Structurizr Lite can also ingest "
"`docs/decisions/` via `!adrs` and render ADRs beside the diagrams, scoped"
" to the software system or container they concern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:109
msgid ""
"Good, because one model generates every view, so Context and Container "
"diagrams cannot contradict each other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:110
msgid ""
"Good, because `!adrs` is the direct answer to \"integrate C4 and ADRs\": "
"decisions become navigable from the element they are about."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:111
msgid ""
"Good, because Structurizr's layout and export options are far better than"
" Mermaid's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:112
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the DSL is still plain text under version control, "
"satisfying that driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:113
msgid ""
"Bad, because it requires running Structurizr Lite (a JVM application, "
"normally via Docker) to see or publish anything, which is a new toolchain"
" for the docs build and for every contributor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:114
msgid ""
"Bad, because rendering into Read the Docs means exporting diagrams as "
"images in CI or hosting a second site — either way the diagram stops "
"being reviewable as a diff."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:115
msgid ""
"Bad, because a central model is maintenance that only pays off at a scale"
" this project has not reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:117
msgid "Option D: Adopt C4 with PlantUML and the C4-PlantUML standard library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:119
msgid ""
"[C4-PlantUML](https://github.com/plantuml-stdlib/C4-PlantUML) provides C4"
" macros for PlantUML, rendered in Sphinx through `sphinxcontrib-"
"plantuml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:121
msgid ""
"Good, because it is the most mature C4 implementation: stable syntax, "
"full element set, good layout control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:122
msgid "Good, because the source stays plain text in the record, like Option B."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:123
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it would sit alongside Mermaid rather than replace it, "
"since the deck and the existing sequence diagrams stay on Mermaid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:124
msgid ""
"Bad, because it adds `sphinxcontrib-plantuml` plus a Java runtime and "
"Graphviz to the documentation build, which Read the Docs must then "
"install on every PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:125
msgid ""
"Bad, because the project would carry two diagram toolchains for one "
"notation, and contributors would have to know which block type to use "
"where."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:127
msgid "More Information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:129
msgid "C4 model: [https://c4model.com/](https://c4model.com/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:130
msgid ""
"Mermaid C4 diagram syntax (flagged experimental): "
"[https://mermaid.js.org/syntax/c4.html](https://mermaid.js.org/syntax/c4.html)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:131
msgid ""
"Structurizr DSL, including `!adrs`: "
"[https://docs.structurizr.com/dsl](https://docs.structurizr.com/dsl)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:132
msgid ""
"C4-PlantUML: [https://github.com/plantuml-"
"stdlib/C4-PlantUML](https://github.com/plantuml-stdlib/C4-PlantUML)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:133
msgid ""
"Sphinx configuration that makes Option B free: `extensions` in "
"[`docs/conf.py`](../conf.py); `sphinxcontrib-mermaid` in the `docs` "
"dependency group of [`pyproject.toml`](../../pyproject.toml)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:134
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Prior art in this repository: the `{mermaid}` block in [ADR-0009](0009"
"-decide-how-to-sync-github-repository-settings-with-terraform.md)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0012-decide-whether-to-adopt-c4-model-diagrams-in-adrs.md:135
msgid ""
"Revisit triggers: Mermaid changing or dropping its C4 syntax; a need for "
"a single model rendered into many synchronized views; or diagrams growing"
" past what Mermaid's layout can present legibly — any of which argues for"
" Option C."
msgstr ""
